            <div xml:id="d764">

                <pb facs="0710" n="704" xml:id="pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1393: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Merriam</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-01-24T12:00:00+02:00">January 24,
                        1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 24—10:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. The three Arabs mentioned in paragraph 1 of my telegram 5, January 23, noon
                    returned to Cairo yesterday bearing the Mufti’s consent to the representation of
                    the Nashashibi Party by two specified delegates. The latter were considered
                    unsuitable by the party heads here who moreover insisted upon the party’s right
                    to choose its own delegates. The party has therefore decided to abstain from the
                    London Conference and not to recognize its findings.</p>
                <p>The Arab delegates minus the Nashashibi sailed for England early this
                    morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Merriam</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
